<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Jan CPI up 3.7 pct m/m, y/y 18.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary Jan CPI up 3.7 pct m/m, y/y 18.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's consumer price index (CPI) was up 3.7 percent in January, compared with 0.9 percent in December, and up 18.9 percent year-on-year, the Central Statistical Office (KSH) said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY'S CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (CPI) -- PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>			 Jan '97	Dec '96	Jan '96</p>
<p> Month-on-month     3.7	    0.9	    4.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year	18.9	   19.8	   28.9</p>
<p>DETAILED CPI PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>				  Jan '97	    Weight in</p>
<p>							   index (pct)</p>
<p>			     mth/mth   yr/yr</p>
<p> Food products	    3.7	 15.7	   28.6</p>
<p>Alcoholic</p>
<p>beverages/</p>
<p>  tobacco products	5.1	 19.5	    9</p>
<p> Clothing		   0.5	 23.4	    6.3</p>
<p>Durable consumer</p>
<p>  goods		     0.6	 10.3	    6.2</p>
<p> Household energy	 2.5	 25.6	    8.0</p>
<p> Other goods, fuels     4.2	 20.1	   17.0</p>
<p> Services		   4.6	 21.0	   24.9</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Total			3.7	 18.9	  100.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Government measures increased the CPI by 1.9 percent month-on-month in January, the KSH said.</p>
<p>These measures included the hikes of consumption tax on vehicle fuel, alcoholic beverages and tobacco, and also the increase in telephone, postal and transport fees, while the consumption tax on coffee, chocolate and gold jewelry was cut.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
